 "last_rtl_message": {
  "stage": "synthesis",
  "visit": 2,
  "text": "DONE. The synthesis gates now pass, but the `stale` check still fails. The failure was a clock-name mismatch in `design.xdc`.\n\n- **Cause:** the flow's default constraint named the reference clock `gt_refclk`, which isn't a declared clock domain. The standards check (STD-CLK-03) flagged it.\n- **Fix:** I added `create_clock -name rclk -period 6.400` on `gt_refclk_p`. That replaces the flow's default and matches the `rclk` domain in `architecture.yaml`.\n- **Clock groups:** I first tried an asynchronous clock group between `sys_clk_pin` and `rclk`. It overrode the XPM Gray and handshake max-delay exceptions and produced 84 CDC findings. I removed it. The XPM macros constrain those crossings themselves.\n- **Check results:** 21 checks pass, congestion is partial (it needs place and route), and fastpath was not run. `build/checks/base/synth.json` has the full report.\n- **Still failing:** `stale` (HDL-ORC-02) says the simulation evidence predates the changes to `design.xdc` and the RTL. Re-running the simulation is outside this stage. It needs a rebuild or re-run of the simulation stage."
 },
